WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.195 --> 00:00:04.235
Hey Youtubers, It's Charlie!

00:00:04.235 --> 00:00:06.215
Thank You everyone that submitted questions for my Doctor Who Q&amp;A

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:11.480
Generally, a lot of questions about what's going on with Clara as well as what's going to be going on in the Christmas Special

00:00:37.499 --> 00:00:42.819
Question 1 - jilly G asks, if The Master had
been saving people’s minds since humans

00:00:42.819 --> 00:00:46.269
first developed concepts of the afterlife,
why didn’t Clara and The Doctor already

00:00:46.269 --> 00:00:50.539
know about 3W? And Do you think they’ll
bring Clara back for the Christmas Special?

00:00:50.539 --> 00:00:55.769
Since almost everyone is asking about Clara
I’ll talk about that first. Yes, I do think

00:00:55.769 --> 00:01:02.769
she’ll appear but I don’t think she’ll
be part of what we saw in the trailer.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:09.700
I think The Doctor will have the ice station
monster storyline and Clara will appear separately.

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.060
There are so many things they still have to
address like Orson Pink. There has to be a

00:01:12.060 --> 00:01:17.329
Danny Pink child in order for their to be
Orson Pink, his grandson to exist.

00:01:17.329 --> 00:01:22.310
It’s possible we could see a super preggo
Clara. If the show moves in real time it would

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:27.420
be less than 9 months. Strax kept going on
and on about fluid retention in the premiere,

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:31.340
and throwing the idea of having children in
Clara’s face all season. It just feels like

00:01:31.340 --> 00:01:35.479
Clara being pregnant would be the most logical
way to wrap those things up.

00:01:35.479 --> 00:01:40.810
As for 3W, you could say that the organization
was incredibly secretive about reaching out

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.610
to the families of the recently deceased.
We didn’t get a scene with Doctor Chang

00:01:44.610 --> 00:01:47.470
meeting with normal people. So we have no
idea how those interactions played out.

00:01:47.470 --> 00:01:51.280
If they just auto-saved people and didn’t
tell the families.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:56.769
The whole 3W thing could have been completely
in Doctor Chang’s head. Like The Master

00:01:56.769 --> 00:02:00.500
fooling him into thinking it was a public
company that did all the things he explained

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.166
in his office with Clara.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.269
Like the company was a fiction in his head,
no one in the real world knew about it. He

00:02:01.269 --> 00:02:02.179
just thought they did because The Master was
messing with his head.

00:02:02.179 --> 00:02:06.829
The less likely explanation is that all The
Master’s changes to the timeline hadn’t

00:02:06.829 --> 00:02:08.569
caught up with Clara and The Doctor yet.

00:02:08.569 --> 00:02:13.720
It feels like characters are able to fool
The Doctor whenever the story requires big

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:17.030
reveals like this. Or something distracts
the Doctor from seeing the very obvious Cyberman

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:17.450
eyes everywhere.

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:23.209
Question 2 - Killer Cookie asks, I don’t
understand why Missy didn’t Regenerate?

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:27.470
I don’t think we’ll get an official explanation
till the next time we see Missy. I would be

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:33.459
amazed if she showed up in the Christmas Special.

00:02:33.459 --> 00:02:38.230
The best theories I’ve seen are that Cyber
Brig’s gun transported her somewhere else

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:43.379
and the Doctor transported her somewhere else
with her Compact the instant before the Brig’s

00:02:43.379 --> 00:02:44.769
gun hit her.

00:02:44.769 --> 00:02:49.989
She’s dematerializing as if she’s not
exploding. A normal cyber blaster would probably

00:02:49.989 --> 00:02:52.590
just have stunned her or caused her to regenerate.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:55.569
The other possibility is that wasn’t the
real Missy on the ground. So that’s why

00:02:55.569 --> 00:02:56.220
she didn’t regenerate.

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:59.849
I kind of like the life model decoy explanation,
the Doctor is a liar, but I do think he was

00:02:59.849 --> 00:03:06.849
ready to kill her. And he was extremely surprised
when the Brig got her first. The salute moment

00:03:12.650 --> 00:03:19.040
felt so sacred that I don’t think Moffat
would take that back by saying the Brig’s

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:20.950
gun transported missy somewhere else.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.269
If you have an alternate theory just write
it in the comments.

00:03:24.269 --> 00:03:29.250
Question 3 - Salem asks, did you notice Clara’s
Eyes in the Opening Sequence?

00:03:29.250 --> 00:03:34.739
I think that was them paying off all the Doctor
Oswald moments in series 8. They’d spent

00:03:34.739 --> 00:03:40.080
multiple scenes with her either pretending
to be The Doctor or doing things that only

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:41.349
The Doctor does.

00:03:41.349 --> 00:03:45.310
It could be part of something bigger but until
we get more information or Moffat explains

00:03:45.310 --> 00:03:49.190
it in an interview I’m going to think of
it as just a one-off thing, just something

00:03:49.190 --> 00:03:50.500
fun.

00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:55.920
Question 4 - Brilchan asks, do you think The
Brig is totally blown up or flying around

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.810
in space now?

00:03:56.810 --> 00:04:02.720
That would be awesome if they did a spinoff
story about the adventures of the Cyber Brig.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:06.700
I think tumblr can help you there, but in
the official canon I think he’s gone in

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:09.590
a cloud of cyber parts.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:13.819
Question 5 - Mitchell asks, do you think Missy
Gave the Doctor the correct coordinates for

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:17.419
Gallifrey and he was just forgetting it was
in another dimension?

00:04:17.419 --> 00:04:23.509
Yes, and also a number of other people in
the comments pointed out that the actual coordinates

00:04:23.509 --> 00:04:28.680
are the same coordinates that The Fourth Doctor
gives up during Pyramids of Mars.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:32.879
So when Missy says it’s where it’s always
been. She’s really being honest.

00:04:32.879 --> 00:04:37.490
Number 6 - Drew asks, what do you think Nick
Frost meant during the Christmas trailer when

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:39.530
he said, “It can’t end like that”?

00:04:39.530 --> 00:04:45.409
I think he’ll force the Doctor to come clean
to Clara and they’ll drop the lies they

00:04:45.409 --> 00:04:50.500
told in a way that will give her run some
closure.

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:57.130
Santa will give them the gift of closure.
Which is all a fan could ever ask for.

00:04:57.130 --> 00:05:04.130
Number 7 - Chaz asks, what do you think about
the controversy over people being upset after

00:05:04.300 --> 00:05:06.160
the last episode?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:12.410
The Don’t Cremate me thing. I usually ignore
stuff like that. I think it was mostly localized

00:05:12.410 --> 00:05:17.639
to the UK. In America stuff like that happens
all the time. Anytime something crazy happens

00:05:17.639 --> 00:05:22.220
on tv or in a movie or a book a small group
of people will always flip their shit and

00:05:22.220 --> 00:05:24.050
scream at broadcasters.

00:05:24.050 --> 00:05:28.300
Anytime I hear people getting upset like that
I just picture the mob from South Park. Where

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:29.080
they all say rabble rabble.

00:05:29.080 --> 00:05:33.020
Number 8 - Danny asks, who’s your favorite
Doctor?

00:05:33.020 --> 00:05:36.650
Right now it’s still Matt Smith followed
closely by David Tennant. I still feel like

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:40.910
it’s too early to put Capaldi into context
with the other Doctor’s. Give him Series

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.870
9 and then I think there will be a better
basis for comparison.

00:05:43.870 --> 00:05:48.770
I always try to keep an open mind about new
actors, especially the secondary actors and

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:49.350
the companions.

00:05:49.350 --> 00:05:55.009
None of them are super sacred to me, I really
enjoy all of them. But I usually watch Doctor

00:05:55.009 --> 00:06:00.030
Who hoping to feel happy. And both Smith and
Tennant made me pretty happy. As opposed to

00:06:00.030 --> 00:06:01.699
depressed or freaked out.

00:06:01.699 --> 00:06:07.669
Number 9 - Dark Neko Studio asks, how possible
is it for Santa Nick Frost to be an exiled

00:06:07.669 --> 00:06:14.669
Time Lord?

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:25.020
Number 10 - Ultimate gamings asks, is Michelle
Gomez Scottish or English?

00:06:50.699 --> 00:06:54.319
There were a couple that asked about Missy’s
Scottish Accent. Just to answer your question

00:06:54.319 --> 00:06:58.800
first. Michelle Gomez was born in Glasgow
just like Peter Capaldi. So I think part of

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:04.229
the reason Missy speaks with a Scottish accent
is because it comes so naturally and on the

00:07:04.229 --> 00:07:05.539
set they thought it worked.

00:07:05.539 --> 00:07:09.910
In the context of the Character, I think The
Master would choose a Scottish accent is because

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:16.910
she’s obsessed with 
The Doctor.

00:07:18.550 --> 00:07:23.330
Based on the first time we see her I think
that The Master regenerated into Missy long

00:07:23.330 --> 00:07:26.960
before the 11th Doctor regenerated into Scottish
12.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:33.960
So it’s a little bit real life influence
and a little bit obsessive Master.

00:07:44.259 --> 00:07:45.419
Winner - Raggedy Girl

